_Data pulled 25 and 26 November 2026 from Ahrefs (UK and US) and checked by hand in UK Google results on 26 November 2026. All traffic figures are Ahrefs estimates, not Meta's analytics._

## At a glance

1. **Facebook Answers went from nothing to about 1.87 million estimated UK Google visits a month in under seven months.** Ahrefs put it at 0 in the week of 4 May 2026 and 1,874,164 on 25 November 2026.
2. **Google's AI cites it. ChatGPT does not.** UK citations on 25 November 2026: 109,237 in AI Overviews, 28,821 in AI Mode, 1,267 in Gemini, 108 in Perplexity and 0 in ChatGPT.
3. **The pages have almost no links.** 3 of the top 30,000 UK URLs by traffic had any referring domain. They probably rank on the strength of the facebook.com domain.
4. **Many rankings did not last.** 4,822 URLs had lost all their estimated traffic in the UK export sorted by traffic change. Another 786 were down.
5. **For UK brands, the lesson is defensive.** The most-cited pages answer basic questions about Premier Inn, Lidl, Costco and Tesco using customer posts. A summary of what strangers said can stand in for your own site when it does not answer those questions clearly.

## What is Facebook Answers? {% #what-it-is %}

Facebook Answers is a directory at facebook.com/fb-answers/. Each page takes one question such as "breakfast timing at Premier Inn" and answers it in a few paragraphs labelled **"Summarized by Meta AI"**. Below the summary the page quotes the public Facebook posts and comments it drew on: hotel branches, group posts, travel bloggers and ordinary users.

Search Engine Roundtable [reported on 5 November 2026](https://www.seroundtable.com/facebook-answers-google-42467.html) that Google had indexed over 6 million of these pages. Saul Westbrook documented the directory and Glenn Gabe called it "another example of massive 'Scaled content abuse'". Most of the coverage so far uses US or worldwide traffic estimates. This post covers the UK and the AI platforms that actually cite the pages.

## How fast did UK traffic grow? {% #uk-growth %}

Ahrefs estimated 0 monthly UK organic visits to the directory in the week of 4 May 2026. The 25 November snapshot showed 1,874,164 visits from 486,210 UK keywords with 142,504 of them in the top 3.

{% chart type="line" eyebrow="UK growth" title="facebook.com/fb-answers/ estimated monthly UK organic traffic, 2026" data="4 May:0|22 Jun:4575|20 Jul:14879|24 Aug:129922|21 Sep:378890|19 Oct:1011485|16 Nov:1601535" source="Ahrefs Site Explorer, GB, weekly history pulled 25 November 2026" /%}

Each point shows Ahrefs' monthly traffic estimate as it stood that week rather than visits in that week. The estimate also jumped to 648,964 in the week of 7 September and fell back to 378,890 two weeks later. It also dipped from 4,575 to 894 between 22 June and 6 July and from about 1.01 million to 855,388 in the week of 26 October. The chart shows roughly every fourth week, so I read those moves as estimate noise rather than events.

| Market | Estimated monthly organic traffic | Keywords | Keywords in top 3 |
|---|---|---|---|
| UK | 1,874,164 | 486,210 | 142,504 |
| US | 12,852,363 | 4,516,136 | 1,590,337 |
| Worldwide | 24,953,826 | 6,719,704 | 2,346,584 |

_Source: Ahrefs Site Explorer, prefix facebook.com/fb-answers/. UK and worldwide 25 November 2026, US 26 November 2026._

The UK is about 7.5% of the worldwide estimate. The US is just over half.

## Which AI platforms cite Facebook Answers? {% #ai-citations %}

**Google's AI cites these pages and ChatGPT almost never does.** I have not seen this split reported elsewhere.

{% chart type="bar" eyebrow="UK AI citations" title="Citations of facebook.com/fb-answers/ pages by AI platform, UK, 25 November 2026" data="AI Overviews:109237|AI Mode:28821|Gemini:1267|Perplexity:108|Copilot:1|ChatGPT:0" highlight="AI Overviews" source="Ahrefs AI responses count, GB, 25 November 2026" /%}

| Platform | UK citations | US citations | Worldwide citations |
|---|---|---|---|
| Google AI Overviews | 109,237 | 339,851 | 1,009,844 |
| Google AI Mode | 28,821 | 146,524 | 458,326 |
| Gemini | 1,267 | 3,959 | 12,304 |
| Perplexity | 108 | 828 | 1,776 |
| Copilot | 1 | 0 | 8 |
| ChatGPT | 0 | 2 | 7 |
| Grok | 0 | 0 | 0 |

_Source: Ahrefs AI responses count, prefix facebook.com/fb-answers/. UK and worldwide 25 November 2026, US 26 November 2026._

Ahrefs also reports an "all platforms" figure of 327,130 UK citations across 271,875 pages. That is more than double the 139,434 the platform rows add up to. The other 187,696 are two further Google counts Ahrefs reports separately, AI Overviews (keywords) and AI Mode (keywords): 163,650 and 24,123 when I re-pulled on 26 November. I use the platform rows above, so the Google figures in this post are the lower of Ahrefs' two counts.

{% stats %}
{% stat value="0" label="ChatGPT citations of fb-answers pages in the UK, against 109,237 in Google AI Overviews" source="Ahrefs AI responses count, GB, 25 November 2026" /%}
{% stat value="3 of 30,000" label="top UK fb-answers URLs by traffic with any referring domain" source="Ahrefs Top pages export, GB, 25 November 2026" /%}
{% /stats %}

Ahrefs data does not show why and I have not tested it. The measurable point is the gap. A single "AI visibility" number would make a source like this one look like an AI search success when almost all of its citations come from Google's AI.

### The AI-cited pages and the traffic pages are mostly different

Only 137 of the top 1,000 UK pages by estimated Google traffic had any AI response citing them. In the US the figure was 168. The pages that get Google clicks (parcel tracking, email logins, school quiz games) are mostly not the pages AI answers cite.

The most-cited UK pages answer basic questions about well-known brands:

| UK page topic | AI responses citing it | Estimated monthly UK traffic |
|---|---|---|
| Premier Inn breakfast times | 40 | 185 |
| JD Sports vs Sports Direct | 28 | 2 |
| Lidl UK online shop | 25 | 72 |
| Costco UK membership eligibility | 25 | 67 |
| Tesco photo printing | 22 | 23 |
| Matalan clothing size chart | 21 | 20 |
| Temu UK warehouse location | 21 | 1,112 |

_Source: Ahrefs Top pages export sorted by AI responses, GB, 25 November 2026. "AI responses" is Ahrefs' "AI responses: All platforms" column for each URL._

The US list has the same shape: Xfinity pricing (70 responses), who can shop at Sally Beauty (52), Buffalo Wild Wings' all-you-can-eat wings (42) and the Bealls senior discount (40). These are opening times, prices and eligibility rules. In each case the brand is the authority on the answer.

## What do the UK results look like? {% #uk-serps %}

Facebook Answers pages appeared in all five UK searches I ran on google.co.uk on 26 November 2026. My results came from a logged-in Chrome session with a Reading location. Your results may differ.

| UK search | fb-answers URLs in the results |
|---|---|
| what time is breakfast at premier inn | 2 |
| evri tracking | 2 |
| temu uk warehouse | 2 |
| costco uk membership requirements | 2 |
| one for all voucher where to spend | 3 (2 in the web results, 1 cited in the AI answer) |

Every search showed at least two different fb-answers pages for the same question. The two Facebook pages for Premier Inn breakfast gave different weekday finishing times in Google's snippets: 10:30am on one and 10am on the other. Premier Inn's own pages ranked above both.

## How stable are the rankings? {% #churn %}

Not very. One UK export covered the top 30,000 rows of Ahrefs' sort by traffic change between its two comparison dates:

- 19,355 URLs were new in that period.
- 4,822 URLs had dropped to zero and lost 265,235 estimated monthly visits between them.
- 5,608 URLs in total had lost traffic with a combined loss of 391,579 estimated visits.

Some of the rankings did not match the page at all. A page about who the Denver Broncos drafted had 8,334 estimated UK visits with "chat gpt login" as its top keyword before it lost them. Two pages about how to say "I love you" in maths had 29,691 estimated visits each with "maths solver" as the top keyword on Malay and Guarani language versions of the URL. Both lost all of it.

Some estimates also look too high. Ahrefs put the Royal Mail tracking page at 142,645 monthly visits although its top keyword has 3,000 searches and ranks at position 11. Treat single-page figures like that with caution. Google's [spam policies](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/essentials/spam-policies#scaled-content) also list scaled content abuse as a violation.

## What this means for UK businesses {% #what-to-do %}

{% panels %}
{% panel eyebrow="Do" title="Answer your own basic questions" tone="good" %}
Publish your opening times, prices, eligibility rules and policies on your own site with one clear answer per question in plain text that Google can read. The most-cited fb-answers pages answer exactly those questions with strangers' posts.
{% /panel %}
{% panel eyebrow="Don't" title="Copy the tactic" tone="bad" %}
These pages probably rank on the strength of the facebook.com domain since they have almost no links of their own. A new site publishing thousands of summarised pages is unlikely to get the same result.
{% /panel %}
{% /panels %}

1. **Search your brand's common questions.** Try "[your brand] opening times", "[your brand] prices" and "[your brand] refund policy" on google.co.uk. See whether an fb-answers page or a third party answers before you do and whether its answer is right.
2. **Check what the AI Overview cites.** Write a better answer on your own page when the AI Overview cites a summary of customer posts instead. The Premier Inn example shows the summaries can disagree with each other.
3. **Measure Google's AI and ChatGPT separately.** This directory gets over 100,000 UK AI Overview citations and none in ChatGPT. A single "AI visibility" figure would hide that. My [UK AI Overviews by industry study](/blog/uk-ai-overviews-by-industry/) breaks the numbers down the same way.

> **Want to know which AI answers cite your business, and which cite someone else?** My [AI Visibility Audit](/ai-visibility/) asks ChatGPT 20 of your buyers' questions three times each and maps the sources it cites.

## Method {% #method %}

- **Section totals and history:** Ahrefs Site Explorer, prefix https://www.facebook.com/fb-answers/, adaptive traffic mode. UK (GB) and worldwide pulled 25 November 2026, US 26 November 2026. Weekly history from 4 May 2026.
- **AI citations:** Ahrefs AI responses count for the same prefix, by platform, on the same dates.
- **Page-level data:** Ahrefs Top pages exports, GB, 25 November 2026 (three exports: sorted by estimated traffic, by AI responses and by traffic change) and US, 26 November 2026 (by traffic and by AI responses). Each export is capped at 30,000 rows. Page counts therefore describe the top 30,000 pages rather than the whole directory. The AI-sorted UK export reached pages with zero AI responses. Its 7,375 cited pages are therefore the full list in that export. Rows are URLs, including the locale language versions of the same page. Ahrefs' domain-level count of UK cited pages is far larger (271,875) because it includes those keyword-based Google counts.
- **Live checks:** five searches on google.co.uk, 26 November 2026, logged-in Chrome, Reading location. Results are personalised and will vary.
- **Limits:** all traffic figures are modelled estimates. Ahrefs' "AI responses" per URL and its domain-level citation counts are different measures and are not mixed in this post. I did not test why ChatGPT does not cite these pages. Ahrefs tracks a different number of prompts on each platform, so the counts are not shares. For scale, it shows 2,926 UK ChatGPT citations for facebook.com as a whole and none for fb-answers.
